{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_015eKAZMSc9HAk9rSLW7nu3W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Written and committed **Q36: What happens when you exceed the context window? How handle long documents?**\n\nKey content in `01-036-what-happens-when-you-exceed-the-context-window-how-handle-l.md`:\n\n- **Concept**: Hard API error or silent truncation at the token limit; O(n²) attention cost makes long contexts expensive even when supported\n- **Mechanism**: Tiered mitigation table — chunking + RAG (default for Q&A), map-reduce summarization (full-doc tasks), sliding windows (transcripts), long-context models (Gemini 1.5 Pro 1M, Claude claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219 200K) as costly fallback\n- **\"Lost in the middle\"**: Liu et al. 2023 — quality degrades for content in the middle of context; mitigation is front-loading/back-loading high-relevance chunks\n- **Pitfalls**: \"Just use a bigger context\" without cost discussion; ignoring lost-in-the-middle; describing chunking without overlap or reranking\n- **Cross-links**: Q5 (context windows), Q14 (chunking), Q44 (lost in the middle)\n\n13 items remaining in the Next queue."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":394,"cache_read_input_tokens":57870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":394,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb6de766-c094-4743-b095-2704ea8727e4","uuid":"457d126f-d7d6-46ab-96db-eb2613b12d66"}
